  "query_preview": "..\nThe Marianas remain on the northern periphery of an unsettled, \ndisorganized pattern. Isolated to patchy scattered showers continue \nto propagate west-northwest through the coastal waters, associated \nwith increased convergence, troughing, and moisture along the\nnorthern edge of a broad, weak disturbance over Yap State. Himawari\nvisible satellite imagery shows a very broad, weak cyclonic turning\ncentered at around 9N142E, to the southeast of Ulithi and Fais in Yap\nState. Models show this weak circulation meandering west-northwest\ntoward Yap Proper over the next day or so, stalling nearby into the\nlatter half of the week. This will maintain a slightly wetter pattern\nfor the Marianas over the next day or two with periods of low-end\nscattered showers and isolated thunderstorms expected through at \nleast Tuesday night. The pattern remains messy and certainty is low \nwith regards to exact coverage and timing of showers, but a drier\npattern is expected to return for the latter half of the week as the\ndisturbance near Yap moves away.",
